---
const items = [
  {
    impact: 'Architectural',
    title: 'A single scalar V_CAL_K cannot generalise across mount positions.',
    body: 'K required to fit gravimetric truth ranged 0.42–1.98 across 11 runs at four mount positions — same chamber, same drip set, same fluid, same board. Eight algorithm variants were trialled (TOP_low, BOT_low, BOT_core, TOP_core, mean-of-pulses, leading-half-pulse, hybrid splash-detector, EMA-adaptive); none passed ±5 % cross-position. Rev-C optics — not Rev-B firmware tweaks — are the path. See §17 in Limitations.',
  },
  {
    impact: 'Fundamental',
    title: 'The mean-of-pulses architecture cannot recover drop oscillation phase.',
    body: 'Drops oscillate between oblate and prolate after detachment (Rayleigh 1879); the chord-time architecture catches each one at an unpredictable phase. The run-mean bias averages out (V_CAL_K = 1.27 works on the run mean) but the per-run residual stays at ±30 %. This is a physics floor of the single-vertical-chord topology, not a tuning problem — recovering phase needs horizontally-separated beam pairs (Rev-C). See §1 in Limitations.',
  },
  {
    impact: 'Methodological',
    title: 'Per-drop bench ground truth needs a closed end-orifice.',
    body: 'The device measures drops at the drip-chamber orifice; the bench scale captures mass at the end-of-tubing orifice. Those two orifices have different surface-tension dynamics — the 2026-05-13 campaign saw end-orifice drop counts 1.5–2× the chamber-drop counts. Per-drop pairing against the scale is therefore invalid; the only valid bench ground truth is the run-mean V_true_chamber = mass / N_UART. Future bench rigs need a catheter-equivalent closed end-orifice for per-drop validation. See §2 in Limitations.',
  },
];

const LIMITATIONS_URL =
  'https://github.com/Gluflex/dripito/blob/v2/docs/limitations.md';
---
<section id="open-questions">
  <div class="eyebrow">Closed by Rev-B</div>
  <h2>What Rev-B proved.</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    Three architectural conclusions Rev-B forced. The next student doesn't
    relitigate these — each is bench-evidenced in
    <a href="#limitations">Limitations</a> and the long form lives in
    <a href={LIMITATIONS_URL} rel="noopener"><code>docs/limitations.md</code></a>.
  </p>

  <ol class="proved-list">
    {items.map((it) => (
      <li class="proved-item">
        <div class="proved-head">
          <h3>{it.title}</h3>
          <span class={`proved-impact proved-impact-${it.impact.toLowerCase()}`}>{it.impact}</span>
        </div>
        <p>{it.body}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
</section>

<style>
  #open-questions {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
  }
  #open-questions h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 40px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  #open-questions a {
    color: var(--ir);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  #open-questions a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .proved-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 36px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .proved-item {
    padding: 22px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--ir);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  }
  .proved-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .proved-head h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .proved-impact {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    padding: 2px 7px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--fg-mute);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .proved-impact-architectural { color: var(--ir);   border-color: var(--ir); }
  .proved-impact-fundamental   { color: var(--ir);   border-color: var(--ir); }
  .proved-impact-methodological { color: var(--flow); border-color: var(--flow); }
  .proved-item p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    #open-questions h2 { font-size: 30px; }
  }
</style>
